    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TfB2nqvpwE54WgLSuyy8aW)_\n\n## What\n\nAn old Zotero export wrote names with a prefix as `biblatex` key=value text, e.g. `family=Hayek given=Friedrich given=Friedrich ..., given=Friedrich A., prefix=von useprefix=false`. This adds a separate operation to `sp-bibtex-lint` that fixes them.\n\n- New command `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-prefixes`, also in `sp-bibtex-lint-convert` (as \"name prefixes\") and as a button in the dry-run report. `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` now lists these entries (with links to the file lines) and counts them.\n- Key=value names (`family=`, `given=`, `prefix=`, `suffix=`, `useprefix=`), also wrapped in braces and in any order:\n  - become the lint's own form, `von Hayek, Friedrich A.` (the module standard is `Last, First`; the existing author fix would turn `Friedrich A. von Hayek` into that anyway)\n  - repeated `given=` parts are merged; a part that fits a longer one (`Friedrich`, `F.` for `Friedrich A.`) is dropped and the fullest stays\n  - `useprefix` is ignored, `suffix` goes in the middle (`Smith, Jr., John`)\n  - names it cannot read (no `family=`, two different families, given names that do not fit) are reported and left as they are\n- Misplaced prefixes in names that already have a comma move in front of the last name: `Hayek, Friedrich A. von`, `Hayek von, Friedrich`, `Hayek, Friedrich A., von` give `von Hayek, Friedrich A.`; `de la` moves together. Only lower-case particles of `sp-bibtex-name-particles` move and one given name always stays (`Li, Bin` is untouched).\n- Same pattern as the other fixes: backup before the first write, batches of `sp-bibtex-lint-batch-size` (50) with apply / skip / drop some / bring back / quit, and now `g` (apply this and all later batches, as in #368). `g` also works in step 1 of the author-name fix. Dropped entries stay out of a global run.\n- Literate doc updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists) and the `.el` tangled from it.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 12 new ERT tests in `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el`: the Hayek example, parts parsing, given-name merging, suffix, particles, field linting, the dry-run report, convert with a backup, batches with `g`, drops. The whole file passes (52/52) on Emacs 29.3 with stubs.\n- Not run on the Mac or on the real `.bib` files; try `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` first.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAEq4doRNBiY7vseha)_",
